SYMEX CRASH (Invariant, symex_assign.cpp assign_from_struct:
`rhs.operands().size() == components.size()`): a NON-template auto
member function returning `__bind_back(*this, __n)` -- the
perfect-forward CTAD chain -- produces a struct assignment whose rhs
operand count differs from the type's component count.  25 lines,
header-free, clang++/g++ accept.  Split from the round-115 ranges
delta-cut (b5); siblings b2/b4 (template callers) fail earlier in the
front end and are recorded in cpp20_ranges_basic_libcxx's desc.

ROUND-117: the CRASH is fixed -- the real defect was a SILENT ESCAPE
from the method-body drain (rethrow -> typecheck_main's uncommitted
catch(int) -> success over a half-cleaned symbol table with code
components still in the object layout).  The drain now recovers silent
escapes through the auditable-incomplete-body tolerance, so this test
currently reports 'could not fully type-check' warnings + vacuous
VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL, matching its KNOWNBUG expectation pattern; it
stays KNOWNBUG because the UNDERLYING failure (operator()'s body
failing to convert, the [dcl.fct]/6 `_Fn...` varargs family recorded in
cpp20_ranges_basic_libcxx) is still open.  Flip when the three-site
varargs fix lands and the assertion verifies non-vacuously.
